.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Raul Ruiz (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Raul Ruiz seeks another term in a Coachella Valley seat that redistricting kept competitive but still tilted Democratic by about four points. He advanced out of the July primary ahead of three Republican rivals, led by Joe Males, and has spent the summer generating local coverage on veterans' legislation, the New River cleanup, and data-center concerns.\n\nThe resource picture is lopsided: Ruiz has raised over $2 million and holds $2.5 million on hand, while Males raised under $1 million and finished with roughly $15,000, with negligible outside spending on either side. Prediction markets price Ruiz around 94 percent. With no general-election polls, the forecast rests on fundamentals and points to a comfortable Ruiz win, with modest uncertainty from the district's swing history.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9829, "margin": 14.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9786, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9843, "margin": 16.0}]}